<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116342" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥριος</span></b>  (A), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Pi.
			<u>P.</u>
			9.98
		</span></i>; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>AP</u>
			7.188
		</span></i> (Thall.), <i><span class="en">
			9.311
		</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
			Phil.
		</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
			Opp.
			<u>H.</u>
			1.689
		</span></i>:—poet. form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡραῖος,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>produced in season,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥρια πάντα</span> all <i>the fruits of
				the season,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.131
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				7.62
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				394
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				15.112
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.329
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> generally,
				<i>in due season, seasonable,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔργα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					392
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				422
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γάμος</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				697
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠδίς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
				</span></i>
			 l.c., cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.311
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Phil.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρόνος ὥ. ἡμῖν</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				10.100
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Antiphan.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλόος κώπαις ὥ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arat.
					154
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥριον</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐστί</span>) c. inf., <i>it is
				time</i> . . , <i><span class="en">
				Sol.
				27.9
			</span></i> (s. v. l.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>youthful,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνθος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
					319
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Philadelphia</span>); <i>fresh,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥριον οἷά τε μῆλον κτλ.</span> Archyt.Amphiss.<i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i> ( =
			<i><span class="en">
				Euph.
				11
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥρια, τά,</span>
			<i>the season,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόσον ὥρια τίκτει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Bion
					<u>Fr.</u>
					15.13
				</span></i>
			.—This poet. form is also used in late Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ὥ. τῆς ἀκμῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
					10.9
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ὥ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.L.
					2.139
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Him.
				<u>Or.</u>
				3.5
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anon.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>; but neut. sg. used as Adv., <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				1076
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θαψάτωσαν καὶ τὰ ὥ. αὐτοῦ, καθὼς
				ἔθος ἐστίν, αὐτοὶ ποιησάτωσαν</span> his <i>funeral
				rites,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				9(1).39
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				42
			</span></i> (Phocis, <span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>).</div>
